{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 (64) code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 (64) code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<iostream>\n#include<algorithm>\n#include<vector>\nusing namespace std;\nusing ll = long long;\nconst ll MOD1 = 998244353, MOD2 = 1000000007;\nconst ll POW10[] = {1, 10, 100, 1000, 10000, 100000, 1000000};\n\nll s[7], ans = 0, cnt1 = 0, n, cnt2 = -1;\nvector<ll> v[7];\n\nvoid dfs1(int depth, ll num) {\n    if (depth == 7) return;\n    v[depth].push_back((cnt1 - num + MOD1) % MOD1);\n    s[depth] = (s[depth] + (cnt1 - num + MOD1) % MOD1) % MOD1;\n    cnt1++;\n    for (int digit = 0; digit <= 9; digit++) {\n        dfs1(depth + 1, num * 10 + digit);\n    }\n}\n\nbool isValid(ll prefix) {\n    return prefix * POW10[6] + 999999 <= n && prefix * POW10[6] * 10 > n;\n}\n\nvoid dfs2(int depth, ll num) {\n    if (num > n) return;\n    if (isValid(num)) {\n        for (int i = 0; i <= 6; i++) {\n            ll target = (cnt2 + 1 - (num * POW10[i])) % MOD1;\n            if (target < 0) target += MOD1;\n            ll idx = lower_bound(v[i].begin(), v[i].end(), MOD1 - target) - v[i].begin();\n            ll part = (s[i] + target * (ll)v[i].size() - MOD1 * ((ll)v[i].size() - idx)) % MOD2;\n            ans = (ans + part) % MOD2;\n        }\n        cnt2 += cnt1;\n        return;\n    }\n    cnt2++;\n    ans = (ans + ((cnt2 - num) % MOD1 + MOD1) % MOD1) % MOD2;\n    for (int digit = (depth == 0 ? 1 : 0); digit <= 9; digit++) {\n        dfs2(depth + 1, num * 10 + digit);\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    cin >> n;\n    dfs1(0, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i <= 6; i++) sort(v[i].begin(), v[i].end());\n    dfs2(0, 0);\n    cout << ans << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport bisect\n\nMOD1 = 998244353\nMOD2 = 1000000007\nPOW10 = [1, 10, 100, 1000, 10000, 100000, 1000000]\n\ns = [0] * 7\nans = 0\ncnt1 = 0\nn = 0\ncnt2 = -1\nv = [[] for _ in range(7)]\n\ndef dfs1(depth, num):\n    global cnt1\n    if depth == 7:\n        return\n    val = (cnt1 - num + MOD1) % MOD1\n    v[depth].append(val)\n    s[depth] = (s[depth] + val) % MOD1\n    cnt1 += 1\n    for digit in range(10):\n        dfs1(depth + 1, num * 10 + digit)\n\ndef isValid(prefix):\n    return prefix * POW10[6] + 999999 <= n and prefix * POW10[6] * 10 > n\n\ndef dfs2(depth, num):\n    global ans, cnt2\n    if num > n:\n        return\n    if isValid(num):\n        for i in range(7):\n            target = (cnt2 + 1 - (num * POW10[i])) % MOD1\n            if target < 0:\n                target += MOD1\n            # Find the index using bisect_left for MOD1 - target\n            idx = bisect.bisect_left(v[i], MOD1 - target)\n            part = (s[i] + target * len(v[i]) - MOD1 * (len(v[i]) - idx)) % MOD2\n            ans = (ans + part) % MOD2\n        cnt2 += cnt1\n        return\n    cnt2 += 1\n    val = ((cnt2 - num) % MOD1 + MOD1) % MOD1\n    ans = (ans + val) % MOD2\n    start_digit = 1 if depth == 0 else 0\n    for digit in range(start_digit, 10):\n        dfs2(depth + 1, num * 10 + digit)